    "text": "Cynthia eats **1 serving of ice cream every night**.  \nShe buys **cartons of ice cream with 15 servings per carton**, at a cost of **$4.00 per carton**.\n\nWe are asked to find out how much she will spend on ice cream after **60 days**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Determine how many servings Cynthia eats in 60 days\n\nSince she eats 1 serving per night:\n\n$$\n\\text{Total servings} = 60 \\text{ days} \\times 1 \\text{ serving/day} = 60 \\text{ servings}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Determine how many cartons she needs\n\nEach carton has 15 servings:\n\n$$\n\\text{Number of cartons} = \\frac{60 \\text{ servings}}{15 \\text{ servings/carton}} = 4 \\text{ cartons}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Calculate the total cost\n\nEach carton costs $4.00:\n\n$$\n\\text{Total cost} = 4 \\text{ cartons} \\times \\$4.00/\\text{carton} = \\$16.00\n$$\n\n---\n\n#### <answer>\n$16.00",
